[0m[0m
In [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m, the [38;5;10mmerge_sort_iteration[0m function used [38;5;10mptr::read[0m + struct assignment to copy sprites between arrays:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// BEFORE (broken) - struct assignment doesn't preserve padding bytes
*b.offset(k as isize) = ptr::read(a.offset(i as isize));
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This caused padding bytes (bytes 12-15 of the 16-byte struct) to contain garbage instead of being preserved from the source. The C code's [38;5;10mb[k] = a[i][0m does a [38;5;10mmemcpy[0m of the full struct including padding.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fixed by using [38;5;10mptr::copy_nonoverlapping[0m which does a byte-exact copy:[0m[0m
[1mrust
[0m[38;5;10m// AFTER (correct) - byte-identical to C's struct assignment
ptr::copy_nonoverlapping(a.offset(i as isize), b.offset(k as isize), 1);
[0m[0m[0m
